  "claim": "The USS Daedalus was named after an exiled Athenian representative of artists from the Minoan civilization.",
  "evidencia": "Page: USS Daedalus (ARL-35). Sentence: Named for Daedalus (in Greek mythology, an exiled Athenian who served in the courts of Minos and Kokalos, regarded as representative of artists and artisans of the later Minoan or Mykenaian age; imprisoned by Minos, he made wings to escape), she was the only U.S. Naval vessel to bear the name.\nPage: Minoan civilization. Sentence: The Minoan civilization was an Aegean Bronze Age civilization on the island of Crete and other Aegean islands which flourished from about 2600 to 1100 BC.\nPage: Minoan civilization. Sentence: It preceded the Mycenaean civilization of Ancient Greece.",
