        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "42ecdf75-dbe1-575a-9e71-3dc36e413181",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Ships: USS Daedalus (ARL-35)\n- People: Daedalus, Minos, Kokalos\n- Civilizations: Minoan civilization, Mycenaean civilization\n- Places: Crete, Aegean islands, Ancient Greece\n- Concepts: Greek mythology, Aegean Bronze Age\n\nFacts:\n- The Minoan civilization was an Aegean Bronze Age civilization on Crete and other Aegean islands that flourished from about 2600 to 1100 BC.\n- The Minoan civilization preceded the Mycenaean civilization of Ancient Greece.\n- In Greek mythology, Daedalus was an exiled Athenian who served in the courts of Minos and Kokalos.\n- In Greek mythology, Daedalus was imprisoned by Minos and made wings to escape.\n- USS Daedalus (ARL-35) was named for Daedalus.\n- USS Daedalus (ARL-35) was the only United States naval vessel to bear the name.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
